WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:02.502 line:0%
JASON: WANT TO PLAY A GAME?

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:06.205 line:0%
WANT TO PLAY A GAME WITH
EVERYONE IN TIMES SQUARE?

00:00:06.472 --> 00:00:08.774 line:0%
<i> [CROWDS CHEERS].</i>

00:00:08.875 --> 00:00:10.776 line:0%
I'M GOING TO GUESS
ABOUT HOW OLD SOMEBODY IS,

00:00:10.876 --> 00:00:12.679 line:0%
WITHOUT EVEN LOOKING AT THEM.

00:00:12.779 --> 00:00:14.013 line:0%
THINK IT'S IMPOSSIBLE?

00:00:14.113 --> 00:00:15.281 line:0%
CHECK THIS OUT.

00:00:15.381 --> 00:00:17.483 line:0%
I'M GOING TO ASK YOU
TO CLOSE YOUR EYES,

00:00:17.584 --> 00:00:19.618 line:0%
AND WHEN I SAY GO,
RAISE UP ONE OF YOUR FEET,

00:00:19.718 --> 00:00:21.821 line:0%
AND TRY TO KEEP YOUR
BALANCE AS LONG AS YOU CAN.

00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:23.456 line:0%
WESTON: ALRIGHT, SOUNDS GOOD.

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:25.191 line:0%
JASON: WANT TO
PLAY ALONG AT HOME?

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:27.359 line:0%
FIND A SAFE SPOT, JUST
IN CASE YOU STUMBLE,

00:00:27.459 --> 00:00:30.663 line:0%
AND GET READY TO CLOSE YOUR
EYES AND PICK UP ONE FOOT.

00:00:30.763 --> 00:00:33.299 line:0%
WE'LL PUT THIS
COUNTER ON YOUR SCREEN.

00:00:33.399 --> 00:00:34.567 line:0%
WHEN YOU PUT YOUR FOOT DOWN,

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:36.836 line:0%
OPEN YOUR EYES
AND CHECK THE TIME.

00:00:36.936 --> 00:00:37.837 line:0%
ARE YOU READY?

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:38.871 line:0%
WESTON: YEAH.

00:00:38.971 --> 00:00:41.607 line:0%
JASON: THREE, TWO, ONE, GO.

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:42.908 line:0%
HIGHER.

00:00:43.008 --> 00:00:44.077 line:0%
LONG AS YOU CAN!

00:00:44.177 --> 00:00:46.378 line:0%
NICE JOB, KEEP IT GOING.

00:00:46.478 --> 00:00:47.814 line:0%
GIRL: THIS IS HARD.

00:00:47.914 --> 00:00:50.816 line:0%
JASON: DOING GREAT,
AAANNNNND.

00:00:50.916 --> 00:00:53.453 line:0%
WHAT ARE YOU LIKE A
YOGI OR SOMETHING?

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:55.354 line:0%
INGLING: I'M ZEN!

00:00:55.454 --> 00:00:59.492 line:0%
FOCUS, I'M GONNA GUESS
YOUR AGE AFTER THIS.

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:02.461 line:0%
TRY NOT TO HOP IF
YOU CAN AVOID IT.

00:01:02.561 --> 00:01:04.330 line:0%
KEEP IT UP, KEEP IT UP,
KEEP IT UP!

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:05.698 line:0%
YOU'RE DOING GOOD!

00:01:05.798 --> 00:01:07.133 line:0%
RACHEL: AHHHH.

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:08.400 line:0%
TRYING TO KEEP IT TOGETHER.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:09.969 line:0%
OH MY GOD, (BLEEP).

00:01:10.069 --> 00:01:11.771 line:0%
JASON: OKAY, TIME'S UP!

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:12.972 line:0%
HOW'D YOU DO?

00:01:13.072 --> 00:01:16.575 line:0%
CAN YOUR SENSE OF BALANCE
REALLY PREDICT YOUR AGE?

00:01:16.675 --> 00:01:20.046 line:0%
SIX SECONDS, YOU'RE BETWEEN
FIFTY FIVE AND SIXTY FIVE.

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:21.747 line:0%
MAN: I'M 59.

00:01:21.848 --> 00:01:23.649 line:0%
JASON: 51 SECONDS,
MY FRIEND.

00:01:23.749 --> 00:01:25.451 line:0%
YOU ARE UNDER TWENTY FIVE.

00:01:25.551 --> 00:01:26.486 line:0%
AND HOW OLD ARE YOU?

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:27.520 line:0%
WESTON: NINETEEN.

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:28.754 line:0%
JASON: ALRIGHT!

00:01:28.854 --> 00:01:30.623 line:0%
YOU LASTED ABOUT 23 SECONDS,
YOU'RE ABOUT 30 YEARS OLD.

00:01:30.723 --> 00:01:31.758 line:0%
AND HOW OLD ARE YOU?

00:01:31.858 --> 00:01:34.293 line:0%
RACHEL: I'M 29.

00:01:34.393 --> 00:01:35.728 line:0%
JASON: WHAT'S GOING ON HERE?

00:01:35.828 --> 00:01:37.363 line:0%
HOW DOES THIS GAME WORK?

00:01:37.463 --> 00:01:40.633 line:0%
STAY TUNED, I'LL GUESS YOUR
AGE AND SHOW YOU HOW YOUR

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:45.138 line:0%
BRAIN USES SENSES
IN ASTONISHING WAYS.

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:47.406 line:0%
JASON: OUR SENSES ARE
HOW WE DECODE AND INTERPRET

00:01:47.506 --> 00:01:49.074 line:0%
WHAT GOES ON AROUND US.

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:52.244 line:0%
AND FOR EVERY ONE OF US,
IT'S A LITTLE DIFFERENT.

00:01:52.344 --> 00:01:55.581 line:0%
OUR SENSES GO WAY
BEYOND BALANCE.

00:01:55.681 --> 00:01:57.182 line:0%
WHY DO SOME OF
US SEE THE WORLD?

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:58.851 line:0%
MAN: THIS ONE MIGHT BE
A LITTLE BIT HEAVIER,

00:01:58.951 --> 00:02:00.486 line:0%
I FEEL LIKE YOU'RE
TRYING TO TRICK ME.

00:02:00.586 --> 00:02:01.887 line:0%
JASON: AND HEAR THE WORLD?

00:02:01.987 --> 00:02:03.856 line:0%
CLAIRE: IT PIERCED
THROUGH MY SOUL.

00:02:03.957 --> 00:02:07.092 line:0%
JASON: AND EXPERIENCE
THE WORLD DIFFERENTLY?

00:02:07.426 --> 00:02:09.295 line:0%
IF WE CAN FOOL OUR SENSES.

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:10.663 line:0%
MAN: I FEEL LIKE
IT'S GETTING BIGGER?

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:12.131 line:0%
I KNOW IT'S NOT RIGHT.

00:02:12.231 --> 00:02:14.567 line:0%
JASON: WHY CAN'T
WE, FINE-TUNE THEM?

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:16.435 line:0%
FARAH: (BLEEP), IT'S SO HARD!

00:02:16.535 --> 00:02:19.505 line:0%
JASON: MASTER THEM, CAN
WE EVEN FIND A NEW SENSE?

00:02:19.605 --> 00:02:22.141 line:0%
COULD WE EVEN
UNLEASH SUPER SENSES?

00:02:22.241 --> 00:02:23.442 line:0%
MAN: WHAAAAT?

00:02:23.542 --> 00:02:25.378 line:0%
NO, THAT'S (BLEEP).

00:02:25.478 --> 00:02:27.847 line:0%
JASON: SO GET READY TO HAVE
SOME SENSE KNOCKED INTO YOU.

00:02:27.947 --> 00:02:29.649 line:0%
ON BRAIN GAMES!

00:02:29.749 --> 00:02:32.886 line:0%
<i> [CROWD CHEERS].</i>

00:02:33.553 --> 00:02:40.059
♪ [THEME MUSIC PLAYS] ♪

00:02:43.996 --> 00:02:45.965 line:0%
THIS IS TIMES
SQUARE IN NEW YORK CITY,

00:02:46.065 --> 00:02:49.301 line:0%
SENSORY OVERLOAD ON STEROIDS.

00:02:50.069 --> 00:02:52.805 line:0%
DISTRACTIONS LEAP OUT AT
US EVERYWHERE WE WALK,

00:02:52.905 --> 00:02:54.473 line:0%
LOOK, OR LISTEN.

00:02:54.573 --> 00:02:56.476 line:0%
IT'S PRETTY MUCH A
MIRACLE THAT OUR BRAINS

00:02:56.576 --> 00:02:59.746 line:0%
DON'T GET OVERWHELMED AND
JUST SHUT DOWN COMPLETELY.

00:02:59.846 --> 00:03:02.214 line:0%
BUT IF YOU HAD TO RELY ON
ONLY THE FIVE BASIC SENSES

00:03:02.314 --> 00:03:06.152 line:0%
IN A PLACE LIKE THIS, YOU
WOULDN'T LAST A MINUTE.

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:09.621 line:0%
YOU KNOW YOUR
FIVE BASIC SENSES, RIGHT?

00:03:09.721 --> 00:03:10.957 line:0%
MAN: WANT ME TO NAME THEM?

00:03:11.057 --> 00:03:14.927 line:0%
ALRIGHT, THERE'S TOUCH,
THERE'S SMELLING, THERE'S...

00:03:15.027 --> 00:03:17.963 line:0%
WOMAN: TASTE, SMELL.

00:03:18.063 --> 00:03:21.901 line:0%
WOMAN 2: SIGHT,
UH, SMELL, TASTE.

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:26.438 line:0%
BOY: TOUCH, TASTE,
SMELL, SIGHT AND HEARING.

00:03:27.106 --> 00:03:28.641 line:0%
JASON: DID YOU
REMEMBER THEM ALL?

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:32.645 line:0%
SIGHT, TOUCH,
SOUND, TASTE, AND SMELL.

00:03:32.745 --> 00:03:34.447 line:0%
THEY'RE THE FIVE
FUNDAMENTAL WAYS YOUR

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:37.216 line:0%
BRAIN RECEIVES INFORMATION.

00:03:37.783 --> 00:03:40.819 line:0%
THESE SENSES MAKE UP
YOUR BRAIN'S CONTROL PANEL

00:03:40.919 --> 00:03:42.287 line:0%
TO THE WORLD.

00:03:42.387 --> 00:03:45.558 line:0%
COMBINE THEM, AND
YOU GET SUPER SENSES.

00:03:45.658 --> 00:03:48.460 line:0%
FOR EXAMPLE, COMBINE
ELEMENTS OF YOUR SENSES:

00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:52.798 line:0%
TOUCH, SIGHT AND SOUND,
AND YOU GET BALANCE,

00:03:52.898 --> 00:03:55.134 line:0%
A SUPER SENSE
YOU USE EVERY DAY,

00:03:55.234 --> 00:03:58.304 line:0%
WITHOUT EVEN
THINKING ABOUT IT.

00:03:59.605 --> 00:04:02.141 line:0%
WE TESTED BALANCE
IN OUR GAME EARLIER.

00:04:02.241 --> 00:04:04.009 line:0%
DO YOU REMEMBER YOUR TIME?

00:04:04.109 --> 00:04:05.978 line:0%
TAKE A LOOK AT THIS CHART.

00:04:06.078 --> 00:04:08.181 line:0%
SCIENCE SAYS
THE OLDER YOU ARE,

00:04:08.281 --> 00:04:09.681 line:0%
THE HARDER THIS GAME IS.

00:04:09.781 --> 00:04:12.317 line:0%
DOES YOUR TIME
MATCH UP WITH YOUR AGE?

00:04:12.417 --> 00:04:16.054 line:0%
AND HOW ARE THESE
PREDICTIONS SO ACCURATE?

00:04:16.155 --> 00:04:18.558 line:0%
KNOWING HOW YOUR BRAIN
CHANGES OVER A LIFETIME,

00:04:18.658 --> 00:04:21.460 line:0%
WE CAN OBSERVE HOW YOUR
SENSES INTERACT WITH THE WORLD,

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:23.629 line:0%
AND PREDICT HOW OLD YOU ARE!

00:04:23.729 --> 00:04:25.498 line:0%
BUT THAT'S JUST THE BEGINNING.

00:04:25.598 --> 00:04:27.433 line:0%
JASON: WE'RE GOING TO DIG
DEEP TO EXPLORE NOT JUST THE

00:04:27.533 --> 00:04:29.068 line:0%
FIVE SENSES YOU KNOW ABOUT,

00:04:29.168 --> 00:04:32.739 line:0%
BUT LOTS OF OTHERS YOU
DIDN'T EVEN REALIZE YOU HAD.

00:04:32.839 --> 00:04:34.640 line:0%
LET'S START WITH A GAME.

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:39.212 line:0%
QUICK, FIND A SEAT AND STICK
YOUR RIGHT FOOT OUT SLIGHTLY.

00:04:39.312 --> 00:04:42.948 line:0%
START TO TURN IT IN
A CLOCKWISE MOTION.

00:04:43.182 --> 00:04:45.551 line:0%
NOW TAKE YOUR RIGHT INDEX
FINGER AND TRY TO DRAW THE

00:04:45.651 --> 00:04:48.121 line:0%
NUMBER SIX FROM
THE TOP DOWN.

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:52.057 line:0%
WHOOPS.

00:04:52.157 --> 00:04:53.226 line:0%
WHAT HAPPENED?

00:04:53.326 --> 00:04:56.028 line:0%
DID YOUR FOOT SUDDENLY
STOP OR CHANGE DIRECTION?

00:04:56.128 --> 00:05:00.432 line:0%
NO MATTER HOW HARD YOU TRY,
YOU PROBABLY CAN'T DO IT.

00:05:00.532 --> 00:05:03.636 line:0%
THE REASON IS BECAUSE THE
LEFT HEMISPHERE OF YOUR BRAIN

00:05:03.736 --> 00:05:06.239 line:0%
CONTROLS THE RIGHT
SIDE OF YOUR BODY.

00:05:06.339 --> 00:05:09.275 line:0%
AND YOUR BRAIN'S MOTOR
CORTEX GIVES INSTRUCTIONS TO

00:05:09.375 --> 00:05:12.144 line:0%
ONLY ONE SIDE OF YOUR BODY
AT THE SAME TIME.

00:05:12.244 --> 00:05:14.347 line:0%
GIVE DIFFERENT DIRECTIONS
TO YOUR RIGHT ARM AND

00:05:14.447 --> 00:05:17.650 line:0%
YOUR RIGHT LEG, AND
YOU'LL GET THE WRONG RESULTS.

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:20.353 line:0%
BUT I WANT TO KNOW: HOW
WE CAN HACK OUR BRAINS AND

00:05:20.453 --> 00:05:23.923 line:0%
USE OUR SENSES TO
DO THE UNEXPECTED?

00:05:24.023 --> 00:05:26.325 line:0%
TO FIND OUT, WE CUSTOMIZED
THIS BIKE WITH A SET OF

00:05:26.426 --> 00:05:29.962 line:0%
DIFFERENTIAL GEARS TO
CONTROL THE HANDLE BARS.

00:05:30.063 --> 00:05:31.697 line:0%
TURN THE
HANDLEBARS TO THE RIGHT,

00:05:31.797 --> 00:05:35.133 line:0%
AND THE BIKE
TURNS TO THE LEFT.

00:05:35.233 --> 00:05:37.503 line:0%
THAT'S NOT SO HARD, RIGHT?

00:05:37.603 --> 00:05:41.974 line:0%
SO, WE TOLD ALL OUR FANS IN
TIMES SQUARE AND OFFERED A

00:05:42.074 --> 00:05:46.278 line:0%
HUNDRED BUCKS TO ANYONE WHO
CAN RIDE THIS BIKE 20 FEET!

00:05:46.379 --> 00:05:48.181 line:0%
WE'LL CHECK IN
WITH THEM LATER.

00:05:48.281 --> 00:05:50.950 line:0%
TO UNDERSTAND WHAT IT WILL
TAKE TO UNLOCK OUR SUPER SENSES,

00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:53.453 line:0%
LET'S START BY TESTING
TWO OF OUR BASIC SENSES

00:05:53.553 --> 00:05:56.222 line:0%
AGAINST EACH
OTHER WITH THIS GAME.

00:05:57.390 --> 00:05:59.524 line:0%
SEE THE TWO DOTS
MOVING ACROSS YOUR SCREEN?

00:05:59.925 --> 00:06:02.895 line:0%
DO THESE DOTS PASS
THROUGH EACH OTHER?

00:06:03.696 --> 00:06:06.399 line:0%
OR DO THEY BOUNCE OFF ONE
ANOTHER AND CHANGE DIRECTION?

00:06:08.467 --> 00:06:09.835 line:0%
WHAT DO YOU THINK?

00:06:10.135 --> 00:06:11.837 line:0%
IT'S HARD TO SAY, RIGHT?

00:06:11.937 --> 00:06:14.306 line:0%
WELL, THIS TIME
PLAY CLOSE ATTENTION.

00:06:14.406 --> 00:06:15.908 line:0%
<i> [CLANG]</i>

00:06:16.008 --> 00:06:17.309 line:0%
A-HA!

00:06:17.409 --> 00:06:19.612 line:0%
CLEARLY THE DOTS
BOUNCE OFF EACH OTHER.

00:06:19.712 --> 00:06:22.248 line:0%
WELL THIS IS WHAT'S
CALLED A CROSS-MODAL ILLUSION,

00:06:23.249 --> 00:06:25.984 line:0%
WHERE ONE SENSE AFFECTS
HOW THE OTHER OPERATES;

00:06:26.084 --> 00:06:27.786 line:0%
IN THIS CASE THE
SOUND OF A COLLISION...

00:06:27.886 --> 00:06:29.755 line:0%
<i> [CLANG]</i>

00:06:29.855 --> 00:06:33.926 line:0%
CHANGES HOW YOUR BRAIN
SEES THE DOTS INTERACT.

00:06:36.229 --> 00:06:39.264 line:0%
THIS IS BECAUSE OUR
SONIC INSTINCTS RUN DEEP.

00:06:39.364 --> 00:06:41.334 line:0%
TO SHOW YOU JUST HOW DEEP,
WE'VE SET UP A LISTENING

00:06:41.434 --> 00:06:44.636 line:0%
STATION WHERE UNSUSPECTING
VOLUNTEERS CAN TEST OUT

00:06:44.736 --> 00:06:46.405 line:0%
A NEW BRAND OF HEADPHONES.

00:06:46.505 --> 00:06:48.073 line:0%
HOST: I WOULD LOVE FOR
YOU TO GIVE ME YOUR HONEST

00:06:48.173 --> 00:06:50.042 line:0%
OPINION ABOUT OUR
NEW HEADPHONES.

00:06:50.143 --> 00:06:51.110 line:0%
WOULD YOU LIKE
TO TRY THEM OUT?

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:52.111 line:0%
MAN: BRING IT, LET'S GO.

00:06:52.211 --> 00:06:53.178 line:0%
HOST: TRY THIS ONE ON.

00:06:53.278 --> 00:06:54.313 line:0%
THROW THEM ON.

00:06:54.413 --> 00:06:55.281 line:0%
CHECK IT OUT.

00:06:55.381 --> 00:06:57.383 line:0%
PICK IT UP.

00:06:59.551 --> 00:07:01.120 line:0%
VOLUNTEER: IT'S SO CLEAR.

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:02.821 line:0%
HOST: EXCELLENT.

00:07:02.921 --> 00:07:05.024 line:0%
VOLUNTEER: OH, I'LL BE JAMMING
ON THE SUBWAY WITH THESE!

00:07:05.124 --> 00:07:06.292 line:0%
HOST: DO IT GIRL, DO IT!

00:07:06.392 --> 00:07:07.793 line:0%
NICE!

00:07:07.894 --> 00:07:09.662 line:0%
JASON: AT FIRST, OUR
VOLUNTEERS ARE PICKING UP

00:07:09.762 --> 00:07:12.164 line:0%
NOTHING BUT GOOD VIBRATIONS.

00:07:12.431 --> 00:07:14.099 line:0%
MAN: LOVE THIS SONG!

00:07:14.199 --> 00:07:18.804 line:0%
YOUNG MAN: BUM, BUM, BUM
AND WHEN YOU TWERK YOU GO,

00:07:18.904 --> 00:07:21.240 line:0%
"BONG BONG BONG BONG."

00:07:21.473 --> 00:07:24.009 line:0%
WOMAN: YEAH, I CAN'T TWERK.

00:07:24.109 --> 00:07:25.912 line:0%
JASON: WHAT THEY DON'T
REALIZE IS WE ARE CONTROLLING

00:07:26.012 --> 00:07:28.848 line:0%
WHAT THEY HEAR
FROM BEHIND THE SET.

00:07:28.948 --> 00:07:30.883 line:0%
BUT WHAT DO YOU THINK
WILL HAPPEN IF WE MIX IN SOME

00:07:30.983 --> 00:07:34.887 line:0%
UNSAVORY SOUNDS, OFFERING UP
A SELECTION OF NOISES RANGING

00:07:34.987 --> 00:07:36.722 line:0%
FROM THE MERELY
OBNOXIOUS TO,

00:07:36.822 --> 00:07:39.291 line:0%
"GET ME THE HECK OUT OF HERE!"

00:07:39.391 --> 00:07:45.531 line:0%
<i> [SCREECHING]</i>

00:07:48.233 --> 00:07:50.269 line:0%
WOMAN: THE NAILS
THAT WERE COMING DOWN.

00:07:50.369 --> 00:07:51.537 line:0%
THAT WAS REALLY WEIRD.

00:07:51.637 --> 00:07:53.472 line:0%
BECAUSE IT WAS LIKE
THE BACK OF MY MOUTH.

00:07:53.572 --> 00:07:55.107 line:0%
THE TEETH WERE LIKE...

00:07:55.207 --> 00:07:58.243 line:0%
<i> [SQUEAK]</i>

00:07:58.343 --> 00:07:59.912 line:0%
WOMAN: NOW IT'S
LIKE A BALLOON.

00:08:00.012 --> 00:08:02.114 line:0%
MAN: OK, MM-HMM.

00:08:02.214 --> 00:08:05.083 line:0%
WOMAN: YOU LOVE THAT ONE,
IS IT SPICE GIRLS?

00:08:05.183 --> 00:08:09.255 line:0%
CLAIRE: IT PIERCED
THROUGH MY SOUL.

00:08:09.355 --> 00:08:12.091 line:0%
CHRIS: OHHHHHHH!!!

00:08:12.191 --> 00:08:14.827 line:0%
CHRIS: THE STYROFOAM STARTS
IN MY BACK AND IT WORKS

00:08:14.927 --> 00:08:18.230 line:0%
ITS WAY UP LIKE THIS, AND
THEN IT COMES UP HERE AND

00:08:18.330 --> 00:08:19.264 line:0%
THEN IT'S IN MY HEAD.

00:08:19.364 --> 00:08:21.100 line:0%
OH, I HATE IT.

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:24.102 line:0%
<i> [DRY HEAVING]</i>

00:08:24.202 --> 00:08:25.570 line:0%
SAKINA: YEAH, I
DON'T LIKE THAT SOUND!

00:08:25.670 --> 00:08:26.538 line:0%
WOMAN: WHAT'S THAT?

00:08:26.638 --> 00:08:27.706 line:0%
SAKINA: IT SOUNDS LIKE SOME...

00:08:27.806 --> 00:08:29.007 line:0%
<i> [WRETCHES].</i>

00:08:29.107 --> 00:08:30.776 line:0%
SORRY, SOMEBODY'S THROWIN' UP!

00:08:30.876 --> 00:08:32.278 line:0%
WHEN I HEARD THE BARF,

00:08:32.378 --> 00:08:35.214 line:0%
I FELT IT IN MY BODY, LIKE
RIGHT HERE IN MY STOMACH.

00:08:35.314 --> 00:08:38.083 line:0%
THAT MADE ME NAUSEOUS.

00:08:38.184 --> 00:08:39.752 line:0%
JASON: SO WHAT'S
GOING ON HERE?

00:08:39.852 --> 00:08:42.321 line:0%
WHY DO WE HAVE SUCH A
PHYSICAL REACTION TO NOTHING

00:08:42.421 --> 00:08:46.025 line:0%
MORE THAN UNPLEASANT NOISE?

00:08:46.125 --> 00:08:47.893 line:0%
HOW DOES YOUR
BRAIN "SENSE" SOUND?

00:08:47.993 --> 00:08:51.297 line:0%
AND WHY DOES IT RESPOND SO
PHYSICALLY TO SOME SOUNDS,

00:08:51.397 --> 00:08:53.633 line:0%
BUT NOT TO OTHERS?

00:08:54.933 --> 00:08:57.235 line:0%
MEASURED IN
SOMETHING CALLED "HERTZ,"

00:08:57.336 --> 00:09:00.038 line:0%
SOUND WAVES MOVE
THROUGH THE AIR AS VIBRATIONS.

00:09:00.138 --> 00:09:04.010 line:0%
THE HIGHER THE FREQUENCY, THE
MORE POWERFUL THE VIBRATIONS.

00:09:06.178 --> 00:09:08.814 line:0%
THE HIGHLY SENSITIVE SYSTEMS
OF YOUR INNER EAR RECEIVE

00:09:08.914 --> 00:09:11.316 line:0%
THESE SOUND WAVES AND
SEND INFORMATION ABOUT THEM

00:09:11.416 --> 00:09:12.818 line:0%
TO YOUR BRAIN.

00:09:12.918 --> 00:09:16.455 line:0%
REMARKABLY, MANY SOUNDS
TRIGGER YOUR AMYGDALA,

00:09:16.555 --> 00:09:18.991 line:0%
THE PART OF YOUR BRAIN THAT
CONTROLS THE "FIGHT OR FLIGHT"

00:09:19.091 --> 00:09:22.360 line:0%
RESPONSE, SUGGESTING OUR
BRAINS HAVE ACTUALLY EVOLVED

00:09:22.461 --> 00:09:24.797 line:0%
TO ASSOCIATE SOUNDS
OF A CERTAIN FREQUENCY,

00:09:24.897 --> 00:09:27.266 line:0%
WITH DANGER OR DISTRESS.

00:09:27.366 --> 00:09:31.137 line:0%
<i> [HORNS HONKING]</i>

00:09:31.237 --> 00:09:32.938 line:0%
JASON: THESE SOUNDS
AREN'T LANGUAGE,

00:09:33.038 --> 00:09:35.040 line:0%
BUT THEY DO COMMUNICATE.

00:09:35.140 --> 00:09:38.043 line:0%
THEY ARE MEANT TO TRIGGER AN
IMMEDIATE BIOLOGICAL RESPONSE.

00:09:38.143 --> 00:09:40.412 line:0%
SO, THOSE SHIVERS YOU
FEEL ARE PROBABLY TIED TO

00:09:40.512 --> 00:09:44.149 line:0%
OUR ANCIENT
SURVIVAL INSTINCT.

00:09:44.383 --> 00:09:47.086 line:0%
EACH OF YOUR SENSES ON ITS
OWN HAS POWERFUL CONNECTIONS

00:09:47.186 --> 00:09:49.421 line:0%
TO YOUR BRAIN, BUT COMBINED,

00:09:49.521 --> 00:09:53.292 line:0%
YOUR SENSES ARE MORE
POWERFUL THAN YOU MIGHT EXPECT.

00:09:53.793 --> 00:09:55.061 line:0%
MAN: OHHH.

00:09:58.964 --> 00:10:01.167 line:0%
JASON: BRAIN GAMES HAS SET
NEW YORK CITY ON A SUPER SENSE

00:10:01.267 --> 00:10:03.202 line:0%
COLLISION COURSE.

00:10:03.302 --> 00:10:07.640 line:0%
WE'VE OFFERED $100 TO ANY OF
OUR FANS IN TIMES SQUARE WHO

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:10.876 line:0%
CAN CONQUER THIS
BACKWARDS BIKE.

00:10:11.476 --> 00:10:12.411 line:0%
JASON: HOW'S YOUR DAY GOING?

00:10:12.511 --> 00:10:13.812 line:0%
CHRIS: SO FAR, SO GOOD.

00:10:13.912 --> 00:10:14.847 line:0%
JASON: HOW OLD ARE YOU?

00:10:14.947 --> 00:10:15.881 line:0%
JABEZ: I'M ELEVEN.

00:10:15.982 --> 00:10:17.316 line:0%
JASON: YOU'RE GONNA BE
RIDING THIS BIKE ABOUT

00:10:17.416 --> 00:10:18.751 line:0%
20 FEET THAT WAY.

00:10:18.851 --> 00:10:20.285 line:0%
IF YOU CAN GET
TO THE OTHER END,

00:10:20.385 --> 00:10:22.854 line:0%
THERE'S A $100 BILL,
NICE AND CRISP THERE,

00:10:22.954 --> 00:10:24.056 line:0%
WAITING FOR YOU.

00:10:24.156 --> 00:10:25.290 line:0%
SERGIO: AND I GET TO KEEP IT?

00:10:25.390 --> 00:10:26.492 line:0%
JASON: YOU GET TO KEEP IT!

00:10:26.592 --> 00:10:27.526 line:0%
WHAT DO YOU DO FOR A LIVING?

00:10:27.626 --> 00:10:28.727 line:0%
JERRY: I'M ACTUALLY
A BIKE COURIER.

00:10:28.827 --> 00:10:30.062 line:0%
JASON: FANTASTIC,
WELL, LISTEN.

00:10:30.162 --> 00:10:31.930 line:0%
THIS MIGHT RESPOND
DIFFERENTLY THAN MOST BIKES,

00:10:32.030 --> 00:10:33.465 line:0%
BUT IT IS MECHANICALLY
POSSIBLE TO RIDE IT.

00:10:33.566 --> 00:10:35.835 line:0%
BUT YOU CAN'T, YOUR FEET
CAN'T TOUCH THE FLOOR.

00:10:35.935 --> 00:10:38.437 line:0%
YOU'VE GOT TO ACTUALLY
RIDE THE BIKE THE WHOLE WAY.

00:10:38.537 --> 00:10:39.705 line:0%
THINK YOU'RE UP
FOR THE CHALLENGE?

00:10:39.805 --> 00:10:40.739 line:0%
CHRIS: I THINK SO.

00:10:40.839 --> 00:10:41.774 line:0%
JASON: ARE YOU READY?

00:10:41.874 --> 00:10:42.808 line:0%
FARAH: OH MY GOD YEAH!

00:10:42.908 --> 00:10:43.843 line:0%
I'M TOTALLY READY.

00:10:43.943 --> 00:10:44.876 line:0%
JASON: LET'S DO THIS!

00:10:44.977 --> 00:10:45.911 line:0%
FARAH: AH!

00:10:46.011 --> 00:10:47.112 line:0%
JASON: HERE YOU GO!

00:10:47.212 --> 00:10:48.147 line:0%
READY?

00:10:48.247 --> 00:10:49.281 line:0%
JABEZ: YES.

00:10:49.381 --> 00:10:50.649 line:0%
JASON: LET'S DO THIS!

00:10:50.749 --> 00:10:52.785 line:0%
JABEZ: WHOA!

00:10:57.923 --> 00:11:01.827 line:0%
JASON: I THINK YOU'VE
GOT TO START AGAIN.

00:11:01.927 --> 00:11:02.894 line:0%
JERRY: REALLY HARD!

00:11:02.994 --> 00:11:04.863 line:0%
JASON: ALRIGHT, GO FOR IT.

00:11:04.963 --> 00:11:07.232 line:0%
<i> [LAUGHTER].</i>

00:11:07.766 --> 00:11:10.202 line:0%
GUY: THIS DOES NOT WORK.

00:11:10.302 --> 00:11:11.537 line:0%
(BLEEP)!

00:11:11.637 --> 00:11:13.205 line:0%
JASON: WHY ISN'T RIDING
THIS BIKE AS EASY AS WELL,

00:11:13.305 --> 00:11:14.407 line:0%
RIDING A BIKE?

00:11:14.507 --> 00:11:16.876 line:0%
EVEN IF YOU KNOW THAT TO
RIDE THE BACKWARDS BIKE YOU

00:11:16.976 --> 00:11:21.047 line:0%
MUST STEER RIGHT TO GO LEFT,
AND LEFT TO GO RIGHT,

00:11:21.147 --> 00:11:25.383 line:0%
IN THE MOMENT YOUR BRAIN
CAN'T HELP BUT REACT WRONG.

00:11:25.617 --> 00:11:27.886 line:0%
LET'S LOOK AT THE ROOT
OF THIS BRAIN FAIL STARTING

00:11:27.986 --> 00:11:29.855 line:0%
WITH A GAME.

00:11:31.590 --> 00:11:34.326 line:0%
TAKE YOUR THUMB AND POINTER
FINGER ON THE HAND YOU USE TO

00:11:34.426 --> 00:11:37.630 line:0%
WRITE WITH, HOLDING THEM ABOUT
A QUARTER OF AN INCH APART,

00:11:37.730 --> 00:11:40.532 line:0%
AS IF YOU WERE GRASPING
A SMALL SCREW OR TACK.

00:11:41.032 --> 00:11:43.936 line:0%
NOW, WITHOUT LOOKING,
GENTLY TOUCH THE NAILS OF

00:11:44.036 --> 00:11:46.872 line:0%
THOSE FINGERS TO THE
TIP OF THE INDEX FINGER ON

00:11:46.972 --> 00:11:48.374 line:0%
YOUR OTHER HAND.

00:11:48.474 --> 00:11:50.943 line:0%
HOW MANY DISTINCT POINTS
OF CONTACT CAN YOU FEEL

00:11:51.043 --> 00:11:53.612 line:0%
ON YOUR FINGER?

00:11:53.712 --> 00:11:55.647 line:0%
DID YOU SAY 2?

00:11:55.747 --> 00:11:59.284 line:0%
NOW, AGAIN WITHOUT LOOKING,
GENTLY TOUCH THOSE FINGERS TO

00:11:59.384 --> 00:12:02.221 line:0%
THE MIDDLE OF THE
OPPOSITE FOREARM.

00:12:02.321 --> 00:12:03.622 line:0%
WHAT DO YOU FEEL NOW?

00:12:03.722 --> 00:12:05.891 line:0%
CAN YOU STILL
DISTINGUISH BOTH FINGERS?

00:12:05.991 --> 00:12:08.293 line:0%
PROBABLY NOT.

00:12:08.393 --> 00:12:10.663 line:0%
THAT'S BECAUSE THERE ARE
FAR FEWER NERVE ENDINGS

00:12:10.763 --> 00:12:13.231 line:0%
NEAR THE SURFACE OF THE
SKIN ON YOUR FOREARM.

00:12:13.332 --> 00:12:15.166 line:0%
THE HIGH CONCENTRATION
OF NERVE ENDINGS IN YOUR

00:12:15.267 --> 00:12:17.436 line:0%
FINGERTIPS SEND TONS
OF DETAILED INFORMATION

00:12:17.536 --> 00:12:21.306 line:0%
TO YOUR BRAIN.

00:12:21.873 --> 00:12:24.543 line:0%
TO SEE JUST HOW
SENSITIVE YOUR SENSES CAN BE,

00:12:24.643 --> 00:12:27.646 line:0%
STANFORD UNIVERSITY'S
DR. ALLISON OKAMURA HAS MET

00:12:27.746 --> 00:12:30.315 line:0%
US IN CENTRAL PARK
TO PLAY A GAME.

00:12:30.415 --> 00:12:32.317 line:0%
DR. OKAMURA: OUR EXPERIENCE OF
OUR OWN BODIES INCLUDES

00:12:32.417 --> 00:12:35.587 line:0%
A LOT OF DIFFERENT SENSES,
LIKE PRESSURE AND TOUCH.

00:12:35.687 --> 00:12:38.690 line:0%
JASON: SHE'S GOT A LOW-TECH
BRAIN HACK DESIGNED TO STIMULATE

00:12:38.790 --> 00:12:42.361 line:0%
YOUR SENSES
AND FOOL YOUR BRAIN.

00:12:42.961 --> 00:12:44.730 line:0%
WITH JUST A CHAIR,
A BLINDFOLD,

00:12:44.830 --> 00:12:48.033 line:0%
AND A RELAXING MASSAGE,
CAN DR. OKAMURA MAKE PEOPLE

00:12:48.133 --> 00:12:50.769 line:0%
QUESTION HOW THEY
"SEE" THEIR OWN BODIES?

00:12:50.869 --> 00:12:52.037 line:0%
DR. OKAMURA:
LET'S GIVE IT A TRY.

00:12:52.137 --> 00:12:55.240 line:0%
I'LL LET YOU PUT THIS ON,
COVER YOUR EYES.

00:12:55.607 --> 00:12:57.475 line:0%
JASON: TO GIVE YOU A SENSE
OF WHAT OUR VOLUNTEERS ARE

00:12:57.575 --> 00:13:01.013 line:0%
ABOUT TO EXPERIENCE,
LET'S PLAY A GAME.

00:13:02.681 --> 00:13:04.683 line:0%
CROSS YOUR INDEX
AND MIDDLE FINGER.

00:13:04.783 --> 00:13:07.385 line:0%
NOW TOUCH THE TIP OR
BRIDGE OF YOUR NOSE WITH THE

00:13:07.485 --> 00:13:10.088 line:0%
SPACE WHERE
YOUR FINGERS CROSS.

00:13:10.188 --> 00:13:13.158 line:0%
DOES IT FEEL LIKE
YOU'RE TOUCHING TWO NOSES?

00:13:13.258 --> 00:13:16.495 line:0%
THIS IS AN EXAMPLE OF WHAT IS
CALLED PERCEPTUAL DISJUNCTION.

00:13:16.595 --> 00:13:19.398 line:0%
YOUR BRAIN DOESN'T EXPECT
YOUR FINGERS TO BE CROSSED,

00:13:19.498 --> 00:13:22.133 line:0%
AND SINCE IT'S RARE FOR THE
OUTSIDE OF BOTH FINGERS TO BE

00:13:22.233 --> 00:13:28.239 line:0%
TOUCHING SOMETHING, YOUR
BRAIN FEELS TWO SEPARATE NOSES.

00:13:28.540 --> 00:13:30.909 line:0%
BELIEVE IT OR NOT, IT WAS
THE ANCIENT GREEK PHILOSOPHER

00:13:31.009 --> 00:13:33.278 line:0%
ARISTOTLE WHO IS SAID
TO HAVE DISCOVERED THIS

00:13:33.378 --> 00:13:36.548 line:0%
LITTLE BRAIN GAME.

00:13:36.648 --> 00:13:38.717 line:0%
AND MORE THAN
2,000 YEARS LATER,

00:13:38.817 --> 00:13:41.686 line:0%
BRAIN HACKS LIKE THIS
ARE STILL GOING STRONG.

00:13:41.786 --> 00:13:43.722 line:0%
ONCE THESE
VOLUNTEERS ARE BLINDFOLDED,

00:13:43.823 --> 00:13:46.792 line:0%
DR. OKAMURA STIMULATES
NERVES IN THEIR ARMS,

00:13:46.892 --> 00:13:50.829 line:0%
WHICH REMARKABLY TRIGGERS
CONFUSION IN THEIR BRAINS.

00:13:50.929 --> 00:13:52.163 line:0%
DR. OKAMURA:
THINK ABOUT YOUR NOSE,

00:13:52.263 --> 00:13:55.000 line:0%
DOES IT FEEL LIKE
IT ALWAYS DOES?

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:57.435 line:0%
JESSE: IT FEELS LIKE MY
NOSE IS GETTING BIGGER.

00:13:57.535 --> 00:13:58.670 line:0%
DR. OKAMURA: OK.

00:13:58.770 --> 00:14:01.173 line:0%
JESSE: I CAN'T HOLD
ONTO MY NOSE ANYMORE.

00:14:01.273 --> 00:14:04.409 line:0%
JASON: WHAT'S HAPPENING
IN OUR VOLUNTEERS' BRAINS?

00:14:04.710 --> 00:14:07.045 line:0%
JESSE: SO I HAD A MENTAL
PICTURE OF ALMOST STANDING

00:14:07.145 --> 00:14:08.113 line:0%
OUTSIDE MY BODY,

00:14:08.214 --> 00:14:10.649 line:0%
WATCHING MY NOSE GROW
AND I TRIED TO KEEP MY

00:14:10.749 --> 00:14:12.050 line:0%
HANDS ON MY NOSE,

00:14:12.150 --> 00:14:13.585 line:0%
BUT I COULDN'T
KEEP IT STEADY,

00:14:13.685 --> 00:14:15.887 line:0%
IT JUST KEPT
ON COMING APART.

00:14:15.987 --> 00:14:17.122 line:0%
DR. OKAMURA:
HOW ABOUT NOW?

00:14:17.222 --> 00:14:19.090 line:0%
ANYTHING?

00:14:19.190 --> 00:14:20.892 line:0%
LITTLE GIRL: IT FEELS BIGGER.

00:14:20.992 --> 00:14:23.762 line:0%
LIKE, LONGER.

00:14:23.862 --> 00:14:25.798 line:0%
TOM: MY NOSE IS
GETTING SKINNY.

00:14:25.898 --> 00:14:27.599 line:0%
KIND OF LONG AND SKINNY.

00:14:27.699 --> 00:14:29.367 line:0%
I'M PINOCCHIO!

00:14:29.467 --> 00:14:30.702 line:0%
DR. OKAMURA: RIGHT!

00:14:30.802 --> 00:14:32.704 line:0%
JASON: SO, WHAT'S
HAPPENING HERE?

00:14:32.804 --> 00:14:34.539 line:0%
WELL, YOU DON'T NORMALLY
HAVE TO KEEP TOUCHING YOUR

00:14:34.639 --> 00:14:37.208 line:0%
NOSE TO KNOW
WHERE IT IS, RIGHT?

00:14:37.309 --> 00:14:39.244 line:0%
THAT'S BECAUSE THE
NERVE ENDINGS IN YOUR SKIN

00:14:39.344 --> 00:14:42.247 line:0%
GIVE YOU A MENTAL MODEL OF
YOUR BODY'S SHAPE AND SIZE.

00:14:42.347 --> 00:14:44.282 line:0%
STIMULATE YOUR
NERVES UNEXPECTEDLY,

00:14:44.383 --> 00:14:48.086 line:0%
AND YOUR BRAIN'S SENSORY
SIGNALS GET SCRAMBLED.

00:14:48.186 --> 00:14:49.755 line:0%
<i> [HEAVY BREATHING].</i>

00:14:49.855 --> 00:14:50.955 line:0%
NICO: OH MY GOSH!

00:14:51.056 --> 00:14:52.524 line:0%
DR. OKAMURA:
WHAT DO YOU FEEL?

00:14:52.624 --> 00:14:53.792 line:0%
NICO: OH MY GOD.

00:14:53.892 --> 00:14:56.795 line:0%
I THINK IT'S GETTING BIGGER,
BUT I KNOW THIS IS NOT RIGHT!

00:14:56.895 --> 00:14:58.763 line:0%
DR. OKAMURA: NOW I'M GOING
TO USE THIS VIBRATION AND

00:14:58.863 --> 00:15:01.233 line:0%
TOUCH UNDERNEATH YOUR ARM.

00:15:01.333 --> 00:15:03.601 line:0%
JASON: STIMULATE AN
OPPOSITIONAL SET OF NERVES,

00:15:03.701 --> 00:15:06.538 line:0%
AND EVEN MORE
SURPRISING THINGS HAPPEN.

00:15:06.638 --> 00:15:10.709 line:0%
<i> [HEAVY BREATHING, LAUGHTER].</i>

00:15:10.809 --> 00:15:12.044 line:0%
NICO: WHOA, MY GOSH.

00:15:12.144 --> 00:15:13.679 line:0%
DR. OKAMURA: DO YOU FEEL
ANYTHING DIFFERENT NOW?

00:15:13.779 --> 00:15:15.381 line:0%
NICO: UH, YEAH, IT
FEELS LIKE MY NOSE IS

00:15:15.481 --> 00:15:17.749 line:0%
KIND OF GETTING SMALLER?

00:15:17.849 --> 00:15:19.284 line:0%
THAT'S NOT POSSIBLE, IS IT?

00:15:19.384 --> 00:15:21.486 line:0%
DR. OKAMURA: MAYBE YOUR
BRAIN IS TELLING YOU SOMETHING.

00:15:21.586 --> 00:15:23.288 line:0%
NICO: I'M STILL
A BIT CONFUSED.

00:15:23.388 --> 00:15:24.923 line:0%
A LITTLE FREAKED OUT.

00:15:25.023 --> 00:15:26.691 line:0%
JASON: MORE THAN JUST
YOUR SENSE OF TOUCH.

00:15:26.791 --> 00:15:28.526 line:0%
THIS IS PROPRIOCEPTION,

00:15:28.626 --> 00:15:30.395 line:0%
SOMETIMES DESCRIBED
AS, "HOW WE FEEL,"

00:15:30.496 --> 00:15:33.932 line:0%
SENSING YOUR BODY'S
POSITION DURING MOVEMENT.

00:15:34.032 --> 00:15:36.835 line:0%
DR. OKAMURA: THESE NEW
SENSATIONS CAN CAUSE US TO

00:15:36.935 --> 00:15:40.205 line:0%
FEEL SOMETHING DIFFERENT
ABOUT OUR OWN BODY SHAPE.

00:15:40.305 --> 00:15:42.307 line:0%
DR. OKAMURA: WHAT MENTAL
PICTURE IS YOUR BRAIN FORMING

00:15:42.407 --> 00:15:44.242 line:0%
OF YOUR BODY RIGHT NOW?

00:15:44.342 --> 00:15:45.411 line:0%
TOM: WITH THIS ONE?

00:15:45.511 --> 00:15:47.179 line:0%
A LITTLE PIGGISH!

00:15:47.279 --> 00:15:48.380 line:0%
DR. OKAMURA: PIGGISH!

00:15:48.480 --> 00:15:49.782 line:0%
YOUR NOSE IS
GETTING SQUASHED, HUH?

00:15:49.882 --> 00:15:52.251 line:0%
TOM: OINK OINK!

00:15:52.351 --> 00:15:54.820 line:0%
JESSE: WOW!

00:15:54.920 --> 00:15:56.154 line:0%
THAT WAS WEIRD!

00:15:56.254 --> 00:15:57.322 line:0%
DR. OKAMURA: RIGHT!

00:15:57.422 --> 00:16:00.259 line:0%
CATARINA: IT'S SURPRISING
THAT THE BRAIN CAN BE TRICKY

00:16:00.359 --> 00:16:01.693 line:0%
WITH YOUR BODY.

00:16:01.793 --> 00:16:03.294 line:0%
DR. OKAMURA: OK, THANK YOU!

00:16:03.394 --> 00:16:04.463 line:0%
CATARINA: THANK YOU.

00:16:04.563 --> 00:16:06.030 line:0%
DR. OKAMURA: ALRIGHT, YOU
CAN TAKE OFF YOUR BLINDFOLD!

00:16:06.130 --> 00:16:08.700 line:0%
CATARINA: THAT'S SO WEIRD.

00:16:08.800 --> 00:16:10.302 line:0%
CATARINA: AMAZING, AMAZING.

00:16:10.402 --> 00:16:12.904 line:0%
JASON: BLINDFOLDED, IT'S
EASY TO SEE HOW PROPRIOCEPTION

00:16:13.004 --> 00:16:16.675 line:0%
IS A SUPER SENSE YOUR BRAIN
MIGHT TAKE FOR GRANTED.

00:16:16.975 --> 00:16:19.511 line:0%
BUT EVEN WITH YOUR EYES WIDE
OPEN YOU MIGHT BE SURPRISED AT

00:16:19.611 --> 00:16:21.813 line:0%
HOW YOUR SENSES CAN BE FOOLED.

00:16:21.913 --> 00:16:24.950 line:0%
LET'S PLAY A GAME TO
SHOW YOU WHAT I MEAN.

00:16:27.452 --> 00:16:29.755 line:0%
WHICH OF YOUR FIVE BASIC
SENSES IS MOST DIRECTLY LINKED

00:16:29.855 --> 00:16:32.090 line:0%
TO YOUR APPETITE?

00:16:32.190 --> 00:16:34.426 line:0%
THE SENSE OF SMELL
IS A COMMON ANSWER.

00:16:34.526 --> 00:16:36.061 line:0%
WELL, IMAGINE YOU'RE HUNGRY.

00:16:36.161 --> 00:16:37.896 line:0%
WHICH OF THESE TWO
PLATES DO YOU THINK YOU'D

00:16:37.996 --> 00:16:40.933 line:0%
CHOOSE FOR A MEAL,
THIS ONE OR THIS ONE?

00:16:43.167 --> 00:16:45.137 line:0%
MOST PEOPLE SAY
THE ONE ON THE RIGHT.

00:16:45.237 --> 00:16:47.005 line:0%
BECAUSE OF THE
SMALLER PLATE SIZE,

00:16:47.105 --> 00:16:49.541 line:0%
YOUR BRAIN MISJUDGES THE
AMOUNT OF FOOD TO BE GREATER,

00:16:49.641 --> 00:16:53.245 line:0%
WHEN IN FACT IT'S THE
SAME AMOUNT ON BOTH PLATES.

00:16:53.512 --> 00:16:56.815 line:0%
THIS VISUAL MISPERCEPTION
OF RELATIVE SIZES IS CALLED A

00:16:56.915 --> 00:17:00.118 line:0%
DELBOEUF ILLUSION, BUT YOU
CAN TURN IT TO YOUR ADVANTAGE.

00:17:00.652 --> 00:17:04.055 line:0%
SWITCHING FROM A 12-INCH
PLATE TO A 10-INCH PLATE

00:17:04.155 --> 00:17:08.026 line:0%
CAN CAUSE YOU TO
CONSUME 22% LESS FOOD.

00:17:08.126 --> 00:17:10.962 line:0%
YOU'LL WASTE LESS TOO
AND YOU'LL EVEN FEEL LIKE

00:17:11.062 --> 00:17:12.831 line:0%
YOU'RE EATING MORE.

00:17:12.931 --> 00:17:15.634 line:0%
WHEN IT COMES TO APPETITE,
SEEING THE FOOD ON YOUR PLATE

00:17:15.734 --> 00:17:19.738 line:0%
IS AS IMPORTANT AS
TASTING OR SMELLING IT.

00:17:19.838 --> 00:17:22.440 line:0%
BUT HOW DOES YOUR SENSE OF
SIGHT MEASURE UP TO TOUCH?

00:17:22.540 --> 00:17:24.643 line:0%
TO FIND OUT WE'VE
INVITED DR. OKAMURA TO

00:17:24.743 --> 00:17:27.879 line:0%
PLAY ANOTHER GAME WITH
US IN LONG ISLAND CITY.

00:17:28.213 --> 00:17:30.948 line:0%
TAKE A LOOK AT
THESE TWO BOXES.

00:17:31.215 --> 00:17:34.019 line:0%
WE'VE PLACED
WEIGHTS INSIDE THEM BOTH.

00:17:34.253 --> 00:17:36.988 line:0%
USING LOGIC AND EXPERIENCE,
YOUR BRAIN MIGHT THINK THE

00:17:37.088 --> 00:17:39.057 line:0%
BIGGER BOX WEIGHS MORE.

00:17:39.157 --> 00:17:41.627 line:0%
RIGHT?

00:17:43.261 --> 00:17:44.696 line:0%
NOW AS YOU CAN SEE
YOU HAVE THESE TWO BLUE BOXES

00:17:44.796 --> 00:17:46.331 line:0%
IN FRONT OF YOU GUYS.

00:17:46.431 --> 00:17:48.600 line:0%
I WANT YOU TO EVALUATE THEM,
JUST KIND OF WALK AROUND AND

00:17:48.700 --> 00:17:49.868 line:0%
GET A SENSE OF
THEIR DIMENSIONS.

00:17:49.968 --> 00:17:51.970 line:0%
STUDY THEM.

00:17:52.070 --> 00:17:53.071 line:0%
ALAIN: SOME BOXES.

00:17:53.171 --> 00:17:54.439 line:0%
COOL.

00:17:54.539 --> 00:17:56.407 line:0%
JASON: NOW ON MY CUE, I'M
GOING TO HAVE YOU LIFT UP THE

00:17:56.507 --> 00:17:57.976 line:0%
BOX IN FRONT OF YOU, AND
JUST GET A SENSE OF ITS WEIGHT.

00:17:58.076 --> 00:17:59.477 line:0%
ALRIGHT, READY?

00:17:59.577 --> 00:18:01.947 line:0%
GO.

00:18:05.116 --> 00:18:06.017 line:0%
ART: OH MAN!

00:18:06.117 --> 00:18:07.819 line:0%
THAT'S HEAVIER THAN I THOUGHT.

00:18:07.919 --> 00:18:08.854 line:0%
EMMA: THIS IS LIGHTER!

00:18:08.954 --> 00:18:11.723 line:0%
I THINK THIS IS LIGHTER.

00:18:12.090 --> 00:18:13.158 line:0%
JASON: SWAP POSITIONS.

00:18:13.258 --> 00:18:14.492 line:0%
FERNANDO:
ALRIGHT, LET'S DO THIS.

00:18:14.592 --> 00:18:16.194 line:0%
JASON: WHEN I SAY
GO, THE SAME THING.

00:18:16.294 --> 00:18:18.564 line:0%
GO.

00:18:19.865 --> 00:18:21.633 line:0%
<i> [ALAIN GRUNTS].</i>

00:18:21.733 --> 00:18:24.936 line:0%
JASON: OUR VOLUNTEERS
CAN'T PEEK INSIDE.

00:18:25.036 --> 00:18:26.571 line:0%
BUT WHICH ONE WAS
HEAVIER TO YOU?

00:18:26.672 --> 00:18:28.907 line:0%
SHIRA: THIS ONE FEELS
A LITTLE BIT HEAVIER.

00:18:29.007 --> 00:18:32.044 line:0%
JASON: BUT THEY'RE ALLOWED
TO LIFT EACH OF THE BOXES.

00:18:32.144 --> 00:18:33.478 line:0%
ALAN: THAT ONE.

00:18:33.578 --> 00:18:34.546 line:0%
JASON: OKAY.

00:18:34.646 --> 00:18:35.681 line:0%
BOTH AGREE?

00:18:35.781 --> 00:18:37.282 line:0%
ALAN: YES, YES.

00:18:37.382 --> 00:18:40.652 line:0%
JASON: DO YOU BOTH AGREE THAT
THE SMALL ONE SEEMS HEAVIER?

00:18:40.752 --> 00:18:41.920 line:0%
ART: OH YEAH.

00:18:42.020 --> 00:18:43.755 line:0%
JONATHAN: CERTAIN,
ABSOLUTELY CERTAIN.

00:18:43.855 --> 00:18:45.390 line:0%
JASON: EVERYONE
SEEMS TO AGREE THE

00:18:45.490 --> 00:18:46.457 line:0%
SMALLER BOX WEIGHS MORE.

00:18:46.558 --> 00:18:47.860 line:0%
TYLER: I FEEL LIKE
YOU'RE TRYING TO TRICK ME!

00:18:51.062 --> 00:18:54.066 line:0%
JASON: WE'VE PLACED WEIGHTS
INSIDE OF EACH OF THESE BOXES.

00:18:54.166 --> 00:18:57.135 line:0%
WE ASKED OUR VOLUNTEERS
WITHOUT PEEKING TO TELL US

00:18:57.235 --> 00:18:59.704 line:0%
WHICH IS HEAVIER.

00:18:59.804 --> 00:19:01.340 line:0%
MAN: THAT ONE
SEEMED HEAVIER.

00:19:01.440 --> 00:19:03.375 line:0%
MAN 2: DEFINITELY,
YEAH, DEFINITELY.

00:19:03.475 --> 00:19:04.877 line:0%
BOY: UH, THIS IS LIGHTER.

00:19:04.977 --> 00:19:06.711 line:0%
WOMAN: YEAH, THIS ONE
FEELS A LITTLE BIT HEAVIER,

00:19:06.811 --> 00:19:08.046 line:0%
WHICH I THOUGHT
IT WOULD BE LIGHTER,

00:19:08.146 --> 00:19:10.481 line:0%
BUT IT'S NOT, I THINK.

00:19:10.581 --> 00:19:12.583 line:0%
HM, LET ME DO IT ONE MORE.

00:19:12.684 --> 00:19:14.819 line:0%
HUH, OKAY.

00:19:14.919 --> 00:19:16.922 line:0%
JASON: SO WHEN YOU
JUST LOOKED AT THE BOXES,

00:19:17.022 --> 00:19:19.358 line:0%
WHEN YOU JUST
LOOKED AT THE SIZE,

00:19:19.458 --> 00:19:20.959 line:0%
WHICH ONE DID YOU
THINK WOULD BE HEAVIER?

00:19:21.059 --> 00:19:22.193 line:0%
ALAIN: UM, I GUESS THIS ONE,

00:19:22.294 --> 00:19:23.762 line:0%
BECAUSE IT WAS
JUST SO BIG, SO.

00:19:23.862 --> 00:19:25.129 line:0%
JASON: WELL IT'S BIGGER, SO.

00:19:25.229 --> 00:19:27.933 line:0%
ALAIN: INITIALLY YOU'RE GOING
TO THINK BIGGER MEANS HEAVIER.

00:19:28.033 --> 00:19:29.934 line:0%
FERNANDO: YEAH, I WAS
THINKING THE SAME THING TOO.

00:19:30.034 --> 00:19:32.237 line:0%
JASON: TURNS OUT THIS GAME
REQUIRES MORE THAN JUST YOUR

00:19:32.337 --> 00:19:34.606 line:0%
SENSE OF SIGHT AND TOUCH.

00:19:34.706 --> 00:19:37.809 line:0%
YOUR BRAIN ALSO
RELIES ON "MOTOR LEARNING,

00:19:37.909 --> 00:19:40.044 line:0%
A KIND OF MUSCLE
MEMORY SUPER SENSE,

00:19:40.144 --> 00:19:42.280 line:0%
TO GAUGE THE
WEIGHT OF THE BOXES.

00:19:42.380 --> 00:19:45.216 line:0%
SO, WHICH BOX IS
REALLY HEAVIER?

00:19:45.316 --> 00:19:46.584 line:0%
JASON: BRING
THAT ONE OVER HERE,

00:19:46.684 --> 00:19:50.923 line:0%
AND THEN READ THE READING
FROM THE SCALE IN POUNDS.

00:19:53.091 --> 00:19:54.225 line:0%
ALAIN: OK, 14 POUNDS.

00:19:54.325 --> 00:19:55.861 line:0%
JASON: 14 POUNDS, ALRIGHT.

00:19:55.961 --> 00:20:00.365 line:0%
SO NOW WE KNOW THE
"LIGHTER" BOX IS 14 POUNDS.

00:20:00.465 --> 00:20:02.334 line:0%
LET'S BRING IN
THE "HEAVIER" BOX.

00:20:02.434 --> 00:20:03.701 line:0%
ALAIN: "HEAVIER BOX."

00:20:03.801 --> 00:20:07.339 line:0%
FERNANDO: ALRIGHT, 14 POUNDS.

00:20:08.406 --> 00:20:09.774 line:0%
<i> [LAUGHTER]</i>

00:20:09.874 --> 00:20:11.143 line:0%
SHIRA: WAIT, WHAT?

00:20:11.243 --> 00:20:12.144 line:0%
JASON: WHAT DOES IT SAY?

00:20:12.244 --> 00:20:15.714 line:0%
SHIRA: 14 POUNDS.

00:20:15.814 --> 00:20:18.550 line:0%
EMMA: 14 POUNDS,
IT'S THE SAME EXACT THING!

00:20:18.650 --> 00:20:23.054 line:0%
BUT, WAIT, WAIT, REALLY?

00:20:23.354 --> 00:20:24.655 line:0%
JASON: YEAH!

00:20:24.756 --> 00:20:27.326 line:0%
EMMA: HOW DOES THAT EVEN
WORK, THOUGH, LIKE, WHY?

00:20:27.426 --> 00:20:29.027 line:0%
DR. OKAMURA: WELL, WHEN
YOU FIRST PICK UP THE BOX,

00:20:29.127 --> 00:20:31.663 line:0%
YOU HAVE THIS EXPECTATION
THAT THE LARGER ONE WILL BE

00:20:31.763 --> 00:20:35.099 line:0%
HEAVIER, AND SO YOU APPLY
MORE FORCE THAN YOU NEED,

00:20:35.199 --> 00:20:38.469 line:0%
AND THAT MAKES IT WIND UP
FEELING LIGHTER IN A WAY.

00:20:38.569 --> 00:20:40.738 line:0%
DR. OKAMURA: BUT YOU
LIFTED IT MULTIPLE TIMES AND

00:20:40.838 --> 00:20:43.508 line:0%
YOU MOVED IT AROUND,
AND YOU REALLY DEVELOPED

00:20:43.608 --> 00:20:46.678 line:0%
AN INTERNAL MODEL OF
WHAT THE WEIGHT WAS.

00:20:46.778 --> 00:20:49.614 line:0%
IN OTHER WORDS YOUR MOTOR
SENSING SYSTEM FIGURED IT OUT.

00:20:49.714 --> 00:20:53.285 line:0%
IT KNOWS THAT IT REQUIRES THE
SAME FORCE TO LIFT EACH BOX.

00:20:53.385 --> 00:20:55.787 line:0%
BUT, THE COGNITIVE,
PERCEPTUAL PART OF YOUR BRAIN

00:20:55.887 --> 00:20:58.089 line:0%
REFUSES TO ACCEPT
THAT CONCLUSION.

00:20:58.189 --> 00:21:02.193 line:0%
SO IT STILL THINKS THAT
THE SMALLER BOX IS HEAVIER.

00:21:02.293 --> 00:21:04.362 line:0%
JASON: WHAT DOES THAT
TELL YOU ABOUT YOUR BRAIN?

00:21:04.462 --> 00:21:05.830 line:0%
EMMA: IT HAS LIED TO ME.

00:21:05.930 --> 00:21:09.167 line:0%
I DO NOT TRUST
ANYTHING, ANYMORE, EVER.

00:21:09.267 --> 00:21:10.935 line:0%
JASON: WE LIVE IN THE MATRIX.

00:21:11.035 --> 00:21:13.971 line:0%
EMMA: OH GOD, NO, WHOO.

00:21:14.071 --> 00:21:17.609 line:0%
JASON: BUT THERE WAS ONE
RESULT I WANT TO LOOK AT AGAIN:

00:21:18.744 --> 00:21:21.179 line:0%
WHEN TWO WEIGHTLIFTERS
TRIED THE EXPERIMENT,

00:21:21.279 --> 00:21:23.281 line:0%
THEY HAD A DIFFERENT
REACTION THAN MOST.

00:21:23.381 --> 00:21:24.316 line:0%
RAYMOND: HOW WAS YOURS?

00:21:24.416 --> 00:21:25.350 line:0%
COMPARE IT TO A PLATE.

00:21:25.450 --> 00:21:26.384 line:0%
TYLER: I FEEL
LIKE THEY'RE CLOSE.

00:21:26.484 --> 00:21:27.418 line:0%
JASON: BUT WHICH ONE
WAS HEAVIER TO YOU?

00:21:27.518 --> 00:21:28.620 line:0%
RAYMOND: I THINK, I THINK,
THEY'RE THE SAME.

00:21:28.720 --> 00:21:29.654 line:0%
TYLER: YEAH.

00:21:29.754 --> 00:21:31.022 line:0%
RAYMOND: AT LEAST TO
ME THEY FELT THE SAME.

00:21:31.122 --> 00:21:32.357 line:0%
JASON: THEY FELT THE SAME?

00:21:32.457 --> 00:21:34.526 line:0%
THEIR EXTRA EXPERIENCE
LIFTING WEIGHTS HELPED THEM

00:21:34.626 --> 00:21:37.995 line:0%
SENSE THE BOXES
WEIGHED EXACTLY THE SAME.

00:21:38.096 --> 00:21:41.933 line:0%
AS THE SAYING GOES,
PRACTICE MAKES PERFECT.

00:21:42.233 --> 00:21:43.935 line:0%
IS THAT WHY PEOPLE IN
TIMES SQUARE ARE HAVING SUCH

00:21:44.035 --> 00:21:46.238 line:0%
A HARD TIME WITH
OUR BACKWARDS BIKE?

00:21:46.338 --> 00:21:50.275 line:0%
<i> [GRUNTS, COMMOTION].</i>

00:21:51.309 --> 00:21:52.944 line:0%
FARAH: (BLEEP), IT'S SO HARD!

00:21:53.044 --> 00:21:55.947 line:0%
JASON: ALRIGHT, GO DIEGO.

00:21:56.047 --> 00:21:58.450 line:0%
MAN: THIS IS NOT WORKING.

00:21:59.117 --> 00:22:01.786 line:0%
<i> [CROWD CHEERS].</i>

00:22:01.886 --> 00:22:04.389 line:0%
JASON: TO HELP EXPLAIN
OUR PEDAL-POWERED PROBLEM

00:22:04.489 --> 00:22:06.524 line:0%
WE TURNED TO DR. ANDY MURRAY,

00:22:06.624 --> 00:22:08.960 line:0%
A NEUROSCIENTIST FROM
COLUMBIA UNIVERSITY.

00:22:09.060 --> 00:22:10.996 line:0%
SO WHAT'S GOING
ON IN THE BRAIN,

00:22:11.096 --> 00:22:13.165 line:0%
WHY ARE PEOPLE GETTING
SO TRIPPED UP TRYING TO

00:22:13.265 --> 00:22:14.399 line:0%
RIDE THIS BIKE?

00:22:14.499 --> 00:22:16.234 line:0%
DR. MURRAY: IF YOU WANT TO
UNDERSTAND NEURAL NETWORKS,

00:22:16.334 --> 00:22:19.270 line:0%
AND WHY IT'S SO DIFFICULT TO
CHANGE A LEARNED MOTOR SKILL,

00:22:19.370 --> 00:22:21.006 line:0%
YOU COULD THINK OF A RIVERBED.

00:22:21.106 --> 00:22:24.309 line:0%
SO INITIALLY WATER FLOWS
IN A COMPLETELY RANDOM WAY,

00:22:24.409 --> 00:22:26.711 line:0%
AND THEN EVENTUALLY IT
STARTS TO FORM A PATH IN THE

00:22:26.811 --> 00:22:28.012 line:0%
SAND AND THE STONES.

00:22:28.113 --> 00:22:29.814 line:0%
AND WATER THAT COMES
AFTER THIS WILL FLOW MUCH

00:22:29.914 --> 00:22:31.216 line:0%
SMOOTHER AND FASTER.

00:22:31.316 --> 00:22:32.650 line:0%
DR. MURRAY: AND
IN THE SAME WAY,

00:22:32.751 --> 00:22:34.319 line:0%
WHEN YOU LEARN A
NEW MOTOR SKILL,

00:22:34.419 --> 00:22:35.887 line:0%
THE FLOW OF INFORMATION
THROUGH YOUR BRAIN IS

00:22:35.987 --> 00:22:37.389 line:0%
INITIALLY RATHER
RANDOM AND CONVOLUTED.

00:22:37.489 --> 00:22:38.723 line:0%
JASON: SURE.

00:22:38.823 --> 00:22:40.358 line:0%
DR. MURRAY: BUT WHEN YOU
REPEAT THAT SKILL OVER AND

00:22:40.458 --> 00:22:42.694 line:0%
OVER AGAIN, THE PATHWAYS
BECOME STRENGTHENED,

00:22:42.794 --> 00:22:44.862 line:0%
AND THE INFORMATION
FLOWS THROUGH THE BRAIN MUCH

00:22:44.962 --> 00:22:46.698 line:0%
FASTER AND SMOOTHER.

00:22:46.798 --> 00:22:48.499 line:0%
JASON: LET'S SEE IF
YOUR BRAIN CAN DEAL WITH

00:22:48.599 --> 00:22:51.236 line:0%
A LITTLE RANDOMNESS.

00:22:51.336 --> 00:22:53.604 line:0%
TAKE THE RANDOM WORDS
WE PUT UP ON SCREEN.

00:22:53.705 --> 00:22:55.841 line:0%
AND MAKE IT INTO A
SENTENCE THAT MAKES SENSE.

00:22:56.574 --> 00:22:57.909 line:0%
GIVE IT A TRY.

00:23:02.313 --> 00:23:05.183 line:0%
DID YOU GET, "TIMES
SQUARE IS VERY BUSY?"

00:23:06.317 --> 00:23:07.753 line:0%
GO AHEAD AND TRY IT AGAIN.

00:23:12.657 --> 00:23:15.594 line:0%
THIS ONE READS,
"LET THE GOOD TIMES ROLL."

00:23:16.394 --> 00:23:17.763 line:0%
NOW FOR ROUND THREE.

00:23:22.100 --> 00:23:24.102 line:0%
THIS TIME YOU
PROBABLY FIGURED OUT,

00:23:24.202 --> 00:23:27.505 line:0%
"LEMON IS THE SOUREST FRUIT."

00:23:27.739 --> 00:23:30.007 line:0%
WAS THIS LAST SENTENCE
EASIER TO UNSCRAMBLE

00:23:30.107 --> 00:23:31.743 line:0%
THAN THE FIRST TWO?

00:23:31.843 --> 00:23:34.345 line:0%
DOING A TASK ONCE AND
LEARNING BASIC DIRECTIONS,

00:23:34.445 --> 00:23:38.116 line:0%
YOUR BRAIN BEGINS TO
CARVE A PATH FOR THIS TASK.

00:23:38.216 --> 00:23:40.952 line:0%
SO, PERHAPS THE BRAIN
BEST-SUITED TO CONQUER OUR

00:23:41.052 --> 00:23:43.588 line:0%
BACKWARDS BIKE WILL BELONG
TO SOMEONE WHO HAS SPENT

00:23:43.688 --> 00:23:45.524 line:0%
YEARS DEDICATED
TO RIDING A BIKE.

00:23:45.624 --> 00:23:46.558 line:0%
JASON: CHARLES.

00:23:46.658 --> 00:23:47.592 line:0%
CHARLES: JASON.

00:23:47.692 --> 00:23:48.860 line:0%
JASON: WELCOME TO BRAIN GAMES.

00:23:48.960 --> 00:23:50.461 line:0%
CHARLES: THANK YOU,
HAPPY TO BE HERE.

00:23:50.561 --> 00:23:51.663 line:0%
JASON: NEUROSCIENTIST
DR. ANDY MURRAY.

00:23:51.763 --> 00:23:53.031 line:0%
CHARLES: NICE TO
MEET YOU, PLEASURE.

00:23:53.131 --> 00:23:56.001 line:0%
JASON: SO, YOU'RE A
PROFESSIONAL BMX RIDER, RIGHT?

00:23:56.101 --> 00:24:00.605 line:0%
CHARLES: RIGHT, I'VE
CYCLED FOR ABOUT 20, 25 YEARS.

00:24:01.473 --> 00:24:02.573 line:0%
JASON: OK.

00:24:02.673 --> 00:24:04.909 line:0%
CHARLES: I RIDE FREESTYLE
BMX, I RIDE FIXED GEAR.

00:24:05.009 --> 00:24:06.411 line:0%
AS A COMMUTER IN THE CITY,

00:24:06.511 --> 00:24:09.647 line:0%
YOU KNOW I DEFINITELY
WAS UP FOR THE CHALLENGE.

00:24:09.881 --> 00:24:12.350 line:0%
JASON: MASTERING THE
BACKWARDS BIKE WON'T BE EASY

00:24:12.450 --> 00:24:14.352 line:0%
EVEN FOR A
PROFESSIONAL BIKE RIDER.

00:24:14.452 --> 00:24:18.022 line:0%
SO, WE GAVE CHARLES THE
BACKWARDS BIKE FOR TWO WEEKS

00:24:18.122 --> 00:24:20.524 line:0%
TO SEE IF HE COULD
REWIRE HIS MOTOR MEMORY WITH

00:24:20.624 --> 00:24:23.194 line:0%
A LITTLE EXTRA TIME.

00:24:23.461 --> 00:24:25.963 line:0%
AND SPEAKING OF TIME,
LET'S PLAY A GAME THAT MIGHT

00:24:26.064 --> 00:24:30.335 line:0%
TURN BACK THE CLOCK USING
ONE OF YOUR SENSES.

00:24:30.802 --> 00:24:34.505 line:0%
LOOK AT THESE IMAGES OF FIVE
POPULAR AND COMMON SCENTS:

00:24:34.739 --> 00:24:39.977 line:0%
CINNAMON, ORANGE, PINE TREE,
PEPPERMINT AND LIME.

00:24:40.978 --> 00:24:43.347 line:0%
NOW WE'RE GOING TO
TAKE THEM AWAY AND LAY THEM

00:24:43.447 --> 00:24:45.851 line:0%
FACE DOWN IN
THE ORIGINAL ORDER.

00:24:47.352 --> 00:24:49.854 line:0%
CAN YOU REMEMBER FROM
JUST A FEW SECONDS AGO WHAT

00:24:49.954 --> 00:24:53.792 line:0%
THE ORIGINAL ORDER WAS?

00:24:57.495 --> 00:24:58.796 line:0%
DID YOU GET IT RIGHT?

00:24:58.897 --> 00:25:00.665 line:0%
WERE YOU ABLE TO
RECALL CINNAMON,

00:25:00.765 --> 00:25:04.102 line:0%
ORANGE, PINE TREE,
PEPPERMINT, THEN LIME?

00:25:04.202 --> 00:25:06.671 line:0%
DID YOU EVEN START TO
SMELL THE SCENT OF THE IMAGES

00:25:06.771 --> 00:25:08.272 line:0%
WE SHOWED YOU?

00:25:08.372 --> 00:25:11.476 line:0%
THIS IS BECAUSE, UNLIKE
TOUCH, SIGHT AND HEARING,

00:25:11.576 --> 00:25:14.979 line:0%
YOUR SENSE OF SMELL HAS
SOME UNIQUE ABILITIES.

00:25:15.246 --> 00:25:17.982 line:0%
YOUR NOSE'S OLFACTORY
BULB IS ACTUALLY PART OF

00:25:18.082 --> 00:25:19.283 line:0%
THE LIMBIC SYSTEM,

00:25:19.383 --> 00:25:22.186 line:0%
WITH INTIMATE ACCESS TO
YOUR HIPPOCAMPUS AND AMYGDALA,

00:25:22.286 --> 00:25:25.590 line:0%
THE PARTS OF YOUR BRAIN MOST
LINKED TO MEMORY AND EMOTION.

00:25:25.690 --> 00:25:28.093 line:0%
YOU MIGHT SAY THE MEMORY OF
THOSE SCENTS TOOK YOU ON A

00:25:28.193 --> 00:25:31.329 line:0%
KIND OF TIME TRAVEL,
RECALLING A WHIFF OF CINNAMON

00:25:31.429 --> 00:25:33.964 line:0%
OR FRESH PINE
EXPERIENCED LONG AGO.

00:25:34.065 --> 00:25:36.434 line:0%
AND HELPING YOU REMEMBER
THE ORDER OF THE CARDS

00:25:36.534 --> 00:25:38.502 line:0%
WE SHOWED YOU.

00:25:38.603 --> 00:25:42.039 line:0%
THIS IS ONE WAY SENSES
AFFECT OUR IDEA OF TIME,

00:25:42.139 --> 00:25:44.842 line:0%
A SUPER SENSE ALL ITS OWN.

00:25:44.942 --> 00:25:47.245 line:0%
AND FOR OUR NEXT GAME,
WE'RE BACK IN TIMES SQUARE

00:25:47.345 --> 00:25:48.946 line:0%
WITH MENTALIST MARC SALEM

00:25:49.046 --> 00:25:52.216 line:0%
TO SEE IF HE CAN
STOP TIME ALL TOGETHER.

00:25:52.316 --> 00:25:53.885 line:0%
MARC: DID IT STOP
WORKING COMPLETELY?

00:25:53.985 --> 00:25:55.387 line:0%
MAN: IT DID.

00:25:58.223 --> 00:26:00.157 line:0%
JASON: QUICK, PAY ATTENTION.

00:26:00.257 --> 00:26:03.127 line:0%
I'M ABOUT TO SHOW YOU A
MAGIC SQUARE WHERE THE NUMBERS

00:26:03.227 --> 00:26:06.131 line:0%
1 THROUGH 9 ARE
ARRANGED SO THAT EVERY ROW

00:26:06.231 --> 00:26:08.165 line:0%
AND EVERY COLUMN,

00:26:08.265 --> 00:26:11.135 line:0%
EVEN THE DIAGONALS
ADD UP TO 15.

00:26:11.236 --> 00:26:13.404 line:0%
BUT THIS IS BRAIN GAMES
SO THERE'S A TWIST.

00:26:13.504 --> 00:26:15.640 line:0%
SOME NUMBERS WILL BE MISSING.

00:26:15.740 --> 00:26:18.476 line:0%
YOU MUST FILL IN
THOSE MISSING NUMBERS.

00:26:18.576 --> 00:26:21.446 line:0%
AND TRY TO KEEP TRACK
OF HOW LONG WE GIVE YOU TO

00:26:21.546 --> 00:26:23.247 line:0%
SOLVE THIS MAGIC SQUARE.

00:26:23.347 --> 00:26:24.249 line:0%
ARE YOU READY?

00:26:24.349 --> 00:26:25.884 line:0%
HERE WE GO.

00:26:33.291 --> 00:26:38.897
♪ ♪

00:26:40.564 --> 00:26:42.032 line:0%
